# Security headers for fauxplane (Doctrine §16.6).
#
# THIS SITE HAS A REAL CONTENT-SECURITY-POLICY, and it is worth saying why that
# was possible here when the hub's own _headers file explains why it was not
# possible there. A CSP is a REFACTOR, not a header: it only works if the page
# carries no inline script and no inline style. This app was written that way
# from the first commit — index.html has no <script> body and no style
# attribute, every module is an external file, and every colour is a custom
# property in styles.css. So `script-src 'self'` costs nothing and is not a
# decoration.
#
# connect-src is 'self' ONLY. Every third-party call goes through a Pages
# Function on this origin (/api/metar, /api/winds, /api/traffic), so the client
# never talks to aviationweather.gov, open-meteo.com or opensky-network.org
# directly. That is the same rule the code follows, enforced by the browser
# rather than by everyone remembering it — and if a later session adds a direct
# fetch, this line is what breaks first.
#
# Permissions-Policy GRANTS what this app genuinely needs and nothing else.
# accelerometer, gyroscope and magnetometer drive the instruments; geolocation
# drives position. Camera is allowed because the ambient-light fallback can use
# a camera frame's luminance — it is never started without an explicit request.
# Everything else is denied outright.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; object-src 'none'
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(self), gyroscope=(self), magnetometer=(self), geolocation=(self), camera=(self), ambient-light-sensor=(self), screen-wake-lock=(self), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=(), midi=(), serial=(), bluetooth=(), display-capture=(), idle-detection=(), interest-cohort=()

# The service worker must not be served from a stale edge cache, or a release
# cannot take effect until the old worker happens to expire.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# The API responses carry their own Cache-Control from the Pages Functions,
# which set it from each source's declared policy. Nothing here overrides them.
